'''Fyresvatnet'''<ref name="name">{{Cite web |title=Informasjon om stadnamn |url=https://stadnamn.kartverket.no/fakta/305148 |access-date=2026-08-09 |website=Norgeskart |publisher=[[Norwegian Mapping Authority|Kartverket]] |language=no}}</ref> is a [[lake]] in [[Fyresdal Municipality]] in [[Telemark]] county, [[Norway]]. With a depth of {{convert|377|m}}, the lake is the [[List of Norwegian Lakes|fifth-deepest lake]] in [[Norway]]. The {{convert|49.7|km2|adj=on}} lake stretches about {{convert|25|km}} from the village of [[Kilegrend]] in the south to [[Moland, Telemark|Moland]] in the north.<ref name="nve" /><ref name="snl">{{Cite SNL|Fyresvatnet|Fyresvatnet|2026-08-09|Lundbo|Sten|2025-06-17|editor2-first=Svein|editor2-last=Askheim}}</ref>

At the southern end of the lake, the sides of the lake are steep and sparsely inhabited. At the north end, near [[Moland Church (Fyresdal)|Moland Church]], the terrain is more open and the residential areas are more dense. This is the site of the village of [[Moland, Telemark|Moland]] (the municipal centre).<ref name="snl" />

Fyresvatnet belongs to the [[Arendal (town)|Arendal]] [[Drainage basin|watershed]], and discharges via the [[Fyresdalsåna]] river into the [[Nidelva (Agder)|Nidelva]] river, which flows into the [[Skagerrak]] at [[Arendal (town)|Arendal]] in [[Agder]] county.

